@startuml arch_hooks
!include palette.iuml
title What do the hooks do around the agent's work?

participant "Agent tool" as tool
participant "session_refresh.py" as refresh
participant "guard_bash.py" as guard
participant "after_edit.py" as edit
participant "git" as git
participant "clang-format" as format

== Claude Code: after a compaction or resume ==
tool -> refresh : payload (cwd, source)
refresh -> git : branch, status,\nlast 5 commits
refresh --> tool : stale-memory reminder\nand git state

== Before a shell command ==
tool -> guard : payload with the command
guard -> guard : split into\nsimple commands
alt a gate bypass or a history rewrite (every tool),\nor any git push outside Claude Code
  guard --> tool : exit 2, reason on stderr
else nothing to block
  guard --> tool : exit 0
end

== After an edit ==
tool -> edit : payload with the file\nand the new text
edit -> edit : find em and\nen dashes
opt C or C++ file with a .clang-format
  edit -> format : format in place
end
alt a dash, or clang-format failed
  edit --> tool : exit 2, report on stderr
else nothing wrong
  edit --> tool : exit 0, notice if reformatted
end

legend right
  Solid arrow: a call
  Dashed arrow: the reply
endlegend
@enduml
